# libretranslate
msgid "**SSO flavor is `oauth2`** (oauth2-proxy sidecar → Keycloak), NOT native OIDC — because Checkmk Raw has no OIDC. The oauth2-proxy authenticates against Keycloak and passes `X-Remote-User`; Checkmk's site Apache trusts it via `auth_by_http_header`. This mirrors [`web-app-openproject`](../../roles/web-app-openproject/)'s header-SSO bridge (`OPENPROJECT_AUTH__SOURCE__SSO_HEADER` + LDAP-gated header trust)."
msgstr "**SSO saveur est `oauth2`** (oauth2-proxy sidecar → Keycloak), NON Natif OIDC — parce que Checkmk Raw n'a pas OIDC. L'aurore2-proxy authentifie contre Keycloak et passes `X-Remote-User`; le site de Checkmk Apache lui fait confiance via `auth_by_http_header`. Ce miroir [`web-app-openproject`](../../roles/web-app-openproject/)'s header-SSO pont (`OPENPROJECT_AUTH__SOURCE__SSO_HEADER` + Confiance d'en-tête liée à LDAP)."

# libretranslate
msgid "**SSO round-trip test:** ``test-oidc-login.js`` drives ``/sso/key/generate`` through the Keycloak login form and asserts the UI no longer falls back to its own password gate."
msgstr "**Essai SSO aller-retour:** ``test-oidc-login.js`` lecteurs ``/sso/key/generate`` via le formulaire de connexion Keycloak et affirme que l'interface utilisateur ne revient plus à sa propre porte de mot de passe."

# libretranslate
msgid "**SSO round-trip test:** `test-oidc-login.js` drives `/sso/key/generate` through the Keycloak login form and asserts the UI no longer falls back to its own password gate."
msgstr "**Essai SSO aller-retour:** `test-oidc-login.js` lecteurs `/sso/key/generate` via le formulaire de connexion Keycloak et affirme que l'interface utilisateur ne revient plus à sa propre porte de mot de passe."

# libretranslate
msgid "**SSO via Keycloak:** configured automatically on first deploy."
msgstr "**SSO via Keycloak:** configuré automatiquement lors du premier déploiement."

# libretranslate
msgid "**SSO via oauth2-proxy with auto-provisioning:** V1 gates all access through the shared Keycloak OIDC client (oauth2-proxy edge). openresty forwards the authenticated identity to n8n as a trusted `Remote-Email` header (`templates/proxy.conf.j2`); an `EXTERNAL_HOOK_FILES` script (`files/hooks.js`, adapted from [PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso](https://github.com/PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso)) reads that header, auto-provisions a local n8n user on first sign-in, and issues n8n's own session cookie — so every Keycloak user lands directly in the workflow editor, with no second, n8n-local login step."
msgstr "**SSO via auth2-proxy avec fourniture automatique:** V1 porte tous les accès via le client Keycloak OIDC partagé (oauth2-arête de proxy). openresty transmet l'identité authentifiée à n8n comme une confiance `Remote-Email` en-tête (`templates/proxy.conf.j2`); une `EXTERNAL_HOOK_FILES` script (`files/hooks.js`, adapté [PavelSozonov/n8n-communauté](https://github.com/PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso)) lit cet en-tête, fournit automatiquement un local n8n utilisateur lors de la première connexion, et numéros n8n cookie de session propre — donc chaque utilisateur Keycloak atterrit directement dans l'éditeur de workflow, sans seconde, n8Étape de connexion n-local."

# libretranslate
msgid "**SSO via oauth2-proxy with auto-provisioning:** V1 gates all access through the shared Keycloak OIDC client (oauth2-proxy edge). openresty forwards the authenticated identity to n8n as a trusted ``Remote-Email`` header (``templates/proxy.conf.j2``); an ``EXTERNAL_HOOK_FILES`` script (``files/hooks.js``, adapted from `PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso <https://github.com/PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso>`__) reads that header, auto-provisions a local n8n user on first sign-in, and issues n8n’s own session cookie — so every Keycloak user lands directly in the workflow editor, with no second, n8n-local login step."
msgstr "**SSO via auth2-proxy avec fourniture automatique:** V1 porte tous les accès via le client Keycloak OIDC partagé (oauth2-arête de proxy). openresty transmet l'identité authentifiée à n8n comme une confiance ``Remote-Email`` en-tête (``templates/proxy.conf.j2``); une ``EXTERNAL_HOOK_FILES`` script (``files/hooks.js``, adapté `PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso <https://github.com/PavelSozonov/n8n-community-sso>`__) lit cet en-tête, fournit automatiquement un local n8n utilisateur lors de la première connexion, et numéros n8Le cookie de session n'est pas propre — donc chaque utilisateur Keycloak atterrit directement dans l'éditeur de workflow, sans seconde, n8Étape de connexion n-local."

# libretranslate
msgid "**SSO** is SuiteCRM's own SAML login against Keycloak (`sso.flavor: saml` in [`meta/services.yml`](./meta/services.yml)), not a proxy in front of it. Unauthenticated requests hit the Symfony firewall's SAML entry point, which redirects to Keycloak; the assertion comes back to `/saml/acs` and establishes a real SuiteCRM session, so the app renders its own authenticated UI including its logout control. Accounts are created on first login from the assertion (`SAML_AUTO_CREATE`), and the IdP signing certificate is read from Keycloak's realm descriptor by [`files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh`](./files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh) at boot, over the Tor SOCKS proxy whenever the issuer is an onion, because a `.onion` issuer is unresolvable directly. `/auth` stays reachable as the local break-glass login."
msgstr "**SSO** est la propre connexion SAML de SuiteCRM contre Keycloak (`sso.flavor: saml` en [`meta/services.yml`](./meta/services.yml))Pas un mandataire devant. Les requêtes non authentifiées touchent le point d'entrée SAML du pare-feu Symfony, qui se redirige vers Keycloak; l'affirmation revient à `/saml/acs` et établit une session SuiteCRM réelle, de sorte que l'application rend son propre UI authentifiée, y compris son contrôle de déconnection. Les comptes sont créés sur la première connexion à partir de l'affirmation (`SAML_AUTO_CREATE`), et le certificat de signature d'IDP est lu à partir du descripteur du royaume de Keycloak par [`files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh`](./files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh) au démarrage, sur le proxy Tor SOCKS chaque fois que l'émetteur est un oignon, parce que `.onion` l'émetteur est insolvable directement. `/auth` reste accessible comme la connexion locale en verre de rupture."

# libretranslate
msgid "**SSO** is SuiteCRM’s own SAML login against Keycloak (``sso.flavor: saml`` in ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__), not a proxy in front of it. Unauthenticated requests hit the Symfony firewall’s SAML entry point, which redirects to Keycloak; the assertion comes back to ``/saml/acs`` and establishes a real SuiteCRM session, so the app renders its own authenticated UI including its logout control. Accounts are created on first login from the assertion (``SAML_AUTO_CREATE``), and the IdP signing certificate is read from Keycloak’s realm descriptor by ```files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh`` <./files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh>`__ at boot, over the Tor SOCKS proxy whenever the issuer is an onion, because a ``.onion`` issuer is unresolvable directly. ``/auth`` stays reachable as the local break-glass login."
msgstr "**SSO** est la propre connexion SAML de SuiteCrms contre Keycloak (``sso.flavor: saml`` en ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__), not a proxy in front of it. Unauthenticated requests hit the Symfony firewall’s SAML entry point, which redirects to Keycloak; the assertion comes back to ``/saml/acs`` and establishes a real SuiteCRM session, so the app renders its own authenticated UI including its logout control. Accounts are created on first login from the assertion (``SAML_AUTO_CREATE``), and the IdP signing certificate is read from Keycloak’s realm descriptor by ```files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh`` <./files/shell/docker-entrypoint.sh>`__ at boot, over the Tor SOCKS proxy whenever the issuer is an onion, because a ``.onion`` issuer is unresolvable directly. ``/auth`` reste accessible comme la connexion locale en verre de rupture."

# libretranslate
