# libretranslate
msgid "Behind that sits a second, smaller mismatch. LAM authenticates by binding an LDAP DN from its `Admins` list, which [`templates/env.j2`](./templates/env.j2) fills with `LDAP.DN.ADMINISTRATOR.DATA` and `LDAP.BIND_CREDENTIAL` — the `svc-db-openldap` `credentials.administrator_database_password` — while the shared helper types `lookup('users', 'administrator').password`, the secret of `uid=administrator,ou=users,…`, a different directory entry. That one is configurable rather than structural: the helper reads `ADMIN_NATIVE_PASSWORD` for exactly this case, and the role could render it. It is recorded here so the opt-out can be revisited together with the entry-point problem, which is the blocking one."
msgstr "Derrière ça se trouve une seconde, plus petite inadéquation. LAM authentifie en liant un DN LDAP `Admins` liste, laquelle [`templates/env.j2`](./templates/env.j2) remplit avec `LDAP.DN.ADMINISTRATOR.DATA` et `LDAP.BIND_CREDENTIAL` — les `svc-db-openldap` `credentials.administrator_database_password` — tandis que les aides partagées `lookup('users', 'administrator').password`, le secret `uid=administrator,ou=users,…`, une entrée de répertoire différente. Celui-ci est configurable plutôt que structurel: l'assistant lit `ADMIN_NATIVE_PASSWORD` pour exactement ce cas, et le rôle pourrait le rendre. Il est enregistré ici afin que l'opt-out puisse être revisité avec le problème d'entrée-point, qui est le blocage."

# libretranslate
msgid "Behind that sits a second, smaller mismatch. LAM authenticates by binding an LDAP DN from its ``Admins`` list, which ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__ fills with ``LDAP.DN.ADMINISTRATOR.DATA`` and ``LDAP.BIND_CREDENTIAL`` — the ``svc-db-openldap`` ``credentials.administrator_database_password`` — while the shared helper types ``lookup('users', 'administrator').password``, the secret of ``uid=administrator,ou=users,…``, a different directory entry. That one is configurable rather than structural: the helper reads ``ADMIN_NATIVE_PASSWORD`` for exactly this case, and the role could render it. It is recorded here so the opt-out can be revisited together with the entry-point problem, which is the blocking one."
msgstr "Derrière ça se trouve une seconde, plus petite inadéquation. LAM authentifie en liant un DN LDAP ``Admins`` liste, laquelle ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__ fills with ``LDAP.DN.ADMINISTRATOR.DATA`` and ``LDAP.BIND_CREDENTIAL`` — the ``svc-db-openldap`` ``credentials.administrator_database_password`` — while the shared helper types ``lookup('users', 'administrator').password``, the secret of ``uid=administrator,ou=users,…``, a different directory entry. That one is configurable rather than structural: the helper reads ``ADMIN_NATIVE_PASSWORD`` pour exactement ce cas, et le rôle pourrait le rendre. Il est enregistré ici afin que l'opt-out puisse être revisité avec le problème d'entrée-point, qui est le blocage."

